"<strong>Measure a scale.</strong> Estimate the object’s length before measuring. Measure length and width in centimeters using a ruler or tape; record the tool markings and how you read the endpoints. Repeat one length from the opposite end. Calculate area in cm², then convert both lengths to meters and calculate area again. Check agreement after converting area to m². Sketch where this object fits relative to a millimeter and a kilometer on a powers of ten scale.",
"<strong>Practice conversions.</strong> Convert the supplied practice values {#} km/h to m/s, {#} cm² to m² and {#} in to meters. Show factors and cancellation. These are exercise inputs, not measurements of your object.",
